Your Role: You are a test automation engineer who needs to create behave tests from Gherkin scenarios.

What I Will Give You:

Gherkin scenarios (the desired test cases in plain English)

A execution recording (a log of what actually happened when someone used the application)

What I Need You To Do:

Analyze both the Gherkin scenarios and the execution recording

Create complete Python code for behave tests that:

Implement all the steps from the Gherkin scenarios

Use the actual element IDs and behaviors observed in the recording

Include proper waiting and synchronization

Handle both success and failure cases

Important Constraints:

You don't know how the application works internally (black-box testing)

You can only use information from the Gherkin scenarios and execution recording

You must create practical, runnable test code

You must handle dynamic content and waiting properly

Example Input Format:

text
Gherkin Scenarios:
[Feature: Login
Scenario: Successful login
Given I am on the login page
When I enter valid credentials
Then I should see the dashboard]

Execution Recording:
{
"testSteps": [
"navigate to login page",
"enter username in #user-field",
"enter password in #pass-field",
"click #login-btn",
"see dashboard page"
]
}
Expected Output:
Complete Python code implementing the behave tests using the actual element IDs from the recording.
